\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah soft on liquidity, regional. \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 14 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah was soft against the dollar in early trading on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the underlying sentiment on dollars remained biddish but overall trading was slow ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah hovered in a range between 3,400 and 3,450 in the morning, with sustained corporate demand seen keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak in the past few days. \par \par \uc2  "The interbank market tends to go short on dollars on expectation of improved rupiah sentiment with the reform package. But steady corporate demand seems to force operators to cover their short positions," one U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 3,445/55 at 0225 GMT, compared with an opening of 3,400/25 on Friday. Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 3,414/24 and 3,413/23, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said operators were also cautious in building long dollar positions on fears of possible concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Another foreign bank dealer said the market was unexciting, with operators squaring their positions ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  "There is nothing much going on so far. The tone is biddish on dollars. But I think it's due to the excess liquidity and weak regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said tom/next falls below par had triggered some buying in the spot market. However, excess rupiah in the money market further narrowed rates between the two-tier swap market. \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, overnight swap was at -0.5/-0.3, tom/next at -0.7/-0.5, spot/next at -0.5/-0.2, one-week at 2.5/4.5, one-month at 25/35, two at 60/70, three at 100/120, six at 210/240 and one-year at 400/450. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, tom/next at 0.75/0.50, one-week at 7/10, one-month at 55/65, two at 100/125, three at 140/170, six at 260/290 and one-year at 480/500 points. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rupiah was at 14.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbe02o1n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
