\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah rebounds on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 14 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah rebounded against the dollar in late trading on Friday following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in as the rupiah fell to touch the day's low of 3,450 in the afternoon following market rumours concerning PT Bank Central Asia (BCA) after a run on deposits at the bank's offices in Medan, north Sumatra. \par \par \uc2  The executive director of Indonesia's Salim Group said on Friday there was no basis for market rumours concerning the group's bank. \par \par \uc2  "The rumours are baseless," group executive director and bank commissioner Benny Santoso told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The rumours ranged from the closure of BCA's offices in Singapore, Malaysia, Hong Kong, to a clearing deficit in Medan, to the death of Salim Group's founder Sudono Salim, one of Indonesia's richest men. \par \par \uc2  However, the Salim Group and PT Bank Danamon later said they had agreed on a partnership, and Credit Suisse First Boston was evaluating a significant equity investment in Bank Danamon, the second largest private bank in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rumours, a run, ample liquidity, weak regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and positive dollar sentiment had sunk the rupiah to the 3,457 level before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't that much but it was effective to correct the market trend because Singapore operators were getting nervous with the BCA rumours," one said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 3,425/35 at 1035 GMT, compared with an opening of 3,400/25 on Friday. Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 3,438.5/42.5 and 3,439.0/43.0, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Santoso said Sudono was in good health and was due take part in an event organised by the PT Indomobil, an automotive company owned by the Salim group, on Friday evening. \par \par \uc2  He said BCA had a representative office in Singapore which was operating as usual. \par \par \uc2  "BCA has only a branch in New York and an affiliate in Hong Kong. Both are also operating as usual," Santoso said. \par \par \uc2  He said it was not true that BCA had suffered a deficit at Friday's clearing in Medan, north Sumatra. \par \par \uc2  "There is also no changes in the shareholders' structure. Everything remains fine and unchanged," he said. \par \par \uc2  Tan Hang Huat, an executive at KMP Private Ltd, one of Salim's private business vehicles said Salim was in Singapore for business and would go back in the late evening. \par \par \uc2  "He comes down for business regularly and he is leaving on SQ 162 (a Singapore Airlines flight) back for Jakarta at 6.30 pm (1030 GMT)," Tan said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rupiah liquidity remained ample in the afternoon, with overnight rates last traded at 14.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, overnight swap was at -0.5/-0.3, tom/next at par/0.1, spot/next at -0.2/0.3, one-week at 4.75/6.75, one-month at 31/35, two at 60/70, three at 95/105, six at 190/220 and one-year at 400/450. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, spot/next was at 0/0.4, tom/next at 0.75/0.50, one-week at 9/15, one-month at 50/70, two at 90/120, three at 140/160, six at 265/290 and one-year at 475/500 points. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbe02k4i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\pic