\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore declines comment on rupiah  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 13 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) said on Thursday it had no comment on market speculation it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets jointly with Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  An MAS spokesman told Reuters the authority had "no comment" on the rumoured \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last week, the MAS confirmed twice that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy rupiah in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in concert with the Bank of Japan and Bank Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese Finance Ministry earlier declined to comment on whether the Bank of Japan was involved in Thursday's rumoured \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah rose to a high of 3,355 to the dollar in early trade on talk Bank Indonesia had sold dollars in Jakarta and Singapore markets above the 3,400 rupiah level. \par \par \uc2  But it drifted back down towards the 3,400 level in afternoon trade on corporate demand for dollars, mainly from Japanese firms, Singapore dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said there was talk Bank Indonesia had been checking rates above the 3,400 level, but it was not clear whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We heard BI had been checking rates for the third time but I'm not sure if they actually sold dollars," a U.S. bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think BI coming in alone would scare the market. It's unlikely they'll have that much effect unless they come in with the Bank of Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore," she added. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbd02lwr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
