\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah steady in slow late trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 7 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah was steady against the dollar in slow late trading on Friday as swap rates edged up slightly, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in briefly, selling dollars from 3,308 to 3,302 level, but met support from Jakarta and offshore fund managers. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 3,290/3,300 at 0900 GMT, compared with an opening of 3,265/95. Dealers said the rupiah was mainly in a range trading between 3,290 and 3,330 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said dollar buying interest from Jakarta was still unabated, aided by relatively ample rupiah. \par \par \uc2  One Singapore-based dealer said there was some dollar buying from fund managers, but the upside was capped by operators in Singapore caught with long dollar positions looking to square their positions ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  He said the arrival of Jakarta players, combined with fund managers buying of dollars, kept the rupiah trading in a narrow range throughout the day. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said fund managers were financing their purchases with funding from the swap market, driving overall swap rates to increase across the curve. \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, swap rates were driven higher due to increases in Singapore market, defying declines in interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rupiah was at 14.0/14.5 percent, with operators still looking for buyers in late afternoon. Tom/next swap was last quoted at 2.25/2.75, one-week at 10/15, one-month at 50/60, two at 75/100, three at 100/130, six at 230/280 and one-year at 430/480 points. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, tom/next swap was at 2.5/3.5, one-week at 35/60, one-month at 115/140, two at 185/215, three at 230/250, six at 330/350 and one-year at 535/565 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was indirectly affected by declines of the Korean Won and the new Taiwan dollars. \par \par \uc2  "It has no direct implication on the Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But people are generally concerned with the on-going crisis over there," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also cautious after another round of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from three central banks on Thursday following the first one on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Some also tried to short the dollar in expectation of the appearance of one of the central banks," one said. \par \par \uc2  The central banks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, the Bank of Japan and Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had said earlier they would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the market was so far unaffected by a bid by Bank Andromeda, part-owned by President Suharto's second son Bambang Trihatmodjo to have a government closure order revoked. \par \par \uc2  Trihatmodjo filed a lawsuit on Wednesday and was followed on Friday by Suharto's half-brother Probosutedjo, whose partly-owned Bank Jakarta was also among the 16 banks shut down. \par \par \uc2  However, State Secretary Murdiono said after meeting with President Suharto on Friday that the government stood behind its decision to liquidate 16 ailing banks. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb702xew\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
