\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Dlr Drops To 3,305 Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 134 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 1997\par 09:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Indonesia, sold the U.S. dollar and bought the rupiah in order to support the local unit, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Indonesia was heard stepping into the market when the dollar was trading around 3,340 rupiah, driving the dollar down to 3,305 rupiah. The dollar, however, bounced back to 3,314 rupiah at 0830 GMT (3:30 a.m. EST). \par \par \uc2  Prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupiah fell to an intraday low of 3,350 per dollar from its close Tuesday at 3,270 on short covering amid dollar-bullishness against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana (62-21) 350-0145 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0838GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb508eqy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
