\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Lower Despite Malaysia Trade Boost \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 1997\par 12:46\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weakened across the board on Wednesday.\par    Both the ringgit and the rupiah fell against the U.S.\par dollar despite the announcement by Malaysia of\par better-than-forecast trade figures for September, and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Among the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , only the Philippine peso\par ended higher. The Thai baht slumped as market participants,\par concerned about King Bhumibol Adulyadej's fragile health\par amid Thailand's current political turbulence, sold baht for\par U.S. dollars.\par    The Singapore dollar also lost ground after the market\par interpreted comments made late Tuesday by Lee Hsien Loong,\par Singapore's deputy prime minister, as indicating the\par government's acceptance of a weaker Singapore dollar.\par    After falling early in the day to an intraday low of\par 3.3330 ringgit to the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar, the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was given a hefty boost in afternoon trading by the\par announcement that Malaysia's September trade surplus reached\par 1.21 billion ringgit, compared with 1.15 billion ringgit for\par August.\par    Maybank, Malaysia's largest bank, was seen buying\par ringgit in volume on the news, sending the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sharply\par higher in a thin market to finish Asian trading hours at\par 3.2800 ringgit to the U.S. dollar, but still slightly lower\par from 3.2650 ringgit at Tuesday's Asian close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-05-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0646EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtb502dq8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
