\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Aid Policy -2: Singapore Dlr Affected \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par 04:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Since the Thai baht was floated in July, the Singapore dollar has fallen 8.5%. \par \par \uc2  'No matter how good Singapore's policy making is, it will still be held hostage to the policy mistakes of neighboring countries,' said Malik. 'The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis shows that Singapore is guilty by association'. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's Foreign Ministry didn't immediately respond to questions on the switch of policy on foreign aid. \par \par \uc2  But Singapore's politicians have admitted that, despite the country's huge \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and healthy economy, that the city state hasn't been untouched by the regional crisis. 'Growth will be slightly slower, but nothing to be alarmed about,' Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong was quoted as saying last week. \par \par \uc2  Manmindar Singh, economist at Nomura Singapore, said financial aid from Singapore could help restore confidence to the southeast Asian region as a whole. \par \par \uc2  Indeed on Monday, the rupiah rallied strongly on news of details of the IMF package for Indonesia and after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore joined the central banks of Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  That boosted the Singapore dollar and the Singapore stock market as well. \par \par \uc2  This higher profile in the Southeast Asian rescue packages has been accompanied by a higher profile for Singapore internationally. Singapore agreed earlier this year to contribute about US$470 million to a new emergency IMF funding mechanism known as the 'New Arrangements To Borrow,' which is expected to total US$50 billion. \par \par \uc2  Impetus for the NAB came after the 1995 bailout for Mexico, which sparked concerns that the IMF might need to raise extra funding quickly, particularly in situations where the U.S. was less motivated to act separately. \par \par \uc2  The NAB will replace an old IMF emergency program that included contributions only from the Group of 10 (G-10) leading industrialized nations. \par \par \uc2  Singapore has also expressed interest in Japan's controversial idea of creating an 'Asia Fund,' though officials have stressed that the facility should be made subordinate to the IMF. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's Goh has also stressed bilateral aid for Indonesia will be contingent on the reform measures agreed with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0337GMT \par \par \uc2  1138 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtb408cp5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
