\par\par \b \uc2  =SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: Rupiah Liquidity Squeezed \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par 13:29\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    U.S. dollar/rupiah swap rates also jumped Tuesday after\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday drained rupiah liquidity from the\par market. At one point during morning trading the one day\par interest rate implied by tomorrow/next U.S. dollar/rupiah\par swap rates reached 175%. It later fell back however, to end\par at 73%. Late Monday the implied rate was at 2.31%.\par    "As long as the central banks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot\par market, they will not let the swap rates come down," said\par the U.K. bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief, explaining the high swap rates\par render it expensive to sell the rupiah short.\par    "We will see this go on for at least another week," he\par predicted. "Any rally (in the U.S. dollar against the\par rupiah) will be met by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the three central\par banks, with Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mopping up any excess liquidity."\par    Elsewhere in Southeast Asia the Malaysian ringgit, the\par Singapore dollar and the Philippine peso strengthened\par against the U.S. dollar, following the regional trend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In subdued trading the ringgit ended at 3.2650 ringgit\par to the U.S. dollar, up from 3.2950 ringgit the previous day.\par    The Singapore dollar closed Asian trading at S$1.5547, up\par from S$1.5558 on Monday, but well down from its intraday\par high of S$1.5445, after domestic banks were seen selling the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Market participants detected the hand of the\par quasi-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore,\par which they said is keen to check the Singapore dollar's\par strength relative to neighboring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Meanwhile, on the Philippine Dealing System the peso\par traded at a weighted average of 34.785 pesos to the U.S.\par dollar, up from 35.144 pesos the previous day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-04-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0729EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtb402ctu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
