\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah stable in range trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 4 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah kept its gains against the dollar in late trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in several times trying to keep the rupiah below the 3,250 level. \par \par \uc2  But swap rates increased in both domestic and offshore markets on fears of tight rupiah liquidity following concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from three central banks on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 3,240/60 at 0950 GMT after hovering in the range between 3,205 and 3,265 throughout the day. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah opened at 3,200/30 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offshore swap rates surged across the curve as operators scrambled for rupiah financing as the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday seemed to have drained rupiah liquidity from the market. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rallied on Monday as central banks of Indonesia, Japan and Singapore rode on momentum sparked by Jakarta's economic reform to support the rupiah. It rose eight percent due to the coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore and Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Swap rates were reflecting Monday's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with rates accelerating upward in the Singapore market. \par \par \uc2  "The market here is feeling the effect now. People are rushing for rupiah liquidity," one Singapore-based dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The two-tier swap market is showing its full effect. Rates offshore have soared," the dealer said, adding the shorter the tenor, the higher were the premiums. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, swap rates remained expensive after easing briefly in early afternoon. Spot/next swap was at 5/10, one-week at 40/60, one-month at 100/140, two at 130/180, three at 190/240, six at 280/320 and one-year at 450/520 points. \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, tom/next swap was at 3.0/4.0, one-week at 15/25, one-month at 45/60, two at 100/130, three at 110/170, six at 270/330 and one-year at 400/500 points. \par \par \uc2  They said the MAS and the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday was placed with Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , causing a drain of rupiah liquidity in the Singapore market which triggered swap rates to increase. \par \par \uc2  One foreign bank dealer said rises in swap rates were more linked to funding purposes rather than mobilisation of funds to prepare for another wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation. \par \par \uc2  Overnight liquidity improved in the afternoon, with overnight rupiah easing to 12/13 percent and some to 16/17 percent. Dealers said operators were keeping ample funds to prepare for any unexpected fall-out from the liquidation of 16 insolvent banks last Saturday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shut down the 16 banks in a move to clean up and strengthen the banking industry. Although the move had been widely expected, people were still nervous of possible follow-through measures on other unhealthy banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also anticipating possible tight rupiah liquidity on Wednesday following concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by three central banks on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Senior traders in Tokyo said the value of concerted dollar sales on Monday was estimated at $300 million to $500 million. \par \par \uc2  They said concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  migh help ease \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  but external debt problem remained to be cleared up in the longer term. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb4037yh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
