\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Indonesian markets mixed on reform package. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Muklis Ali \par \uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 1997\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 3 (Reuters) - The rupiah surged against the dollar on Monday in the wake of economic reforms planned by the government and coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by monetary authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan and Singapore, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But the Jakarta share market was lukewarm, rising initially in line with the rupiah, but falling back before ending slightly up in a volatile trading day, stockbrokers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the eight percent recovery in the rupiah against the dollar in a single day was also helped by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of Japan (BOJ), the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) and Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is riding on the positive momentum that was caused by the announcement of the reforms," said Vincent Low, fixed-income strategist of Merrill Lynch in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  However, the IMF-led economic package failed to ignite a sustainable rally in the stock market. The composite of 277 companies edged up 0.26 percent to close at 501.71 points. \par \par \uc2  The market opened with a jump of almost three percent on local-led speculative buying in banking shares, but failed to trigger a follow-through from offshore investors. \par \par \uc2  "There is no major response from investors although the package is positive in the long-run. I think people are still waiting for more details on the package," said Stephanus Partono, an analyst with Goldman Sachs in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "We maintain a neutral weighting as we do not expect a major rally in the market. The regional markets are still weak and the Indonesian economy is likely to slow down," he said. \par \par \uc2  Partono said investors were also waiting to see whether the rupiah could hold on to newly gained territory against the dollar. "What the market needs is rupiah stability." \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad said Bank Indonesia had acted in concert with Singapore and Japan on Monday to support the rupiah. The finance ministries of Singapore and Japan also said that they had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to show confidence in the macroeconomic policies of the Indonesian government. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended at 3,270/3,000 against the dollar in Jakarta, compared with an opening of 3,550. The rupiah fell to a historic low of 3,850 on October 6. \par \par \uc2  "Today's concerted effort was aimed at strengthening the rupiah to levels more appropriate with the fundamentals of the Indonesian economy," Mar'ie said. \par \par \uc2  "The three authorities also confirmed that they stand ready to take steps necessary in the future to maintain stability of the rupiah as a part of stabilising \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region." \par \par \uc2  Mar'ie said this effort would contribute positively to the implementation of the assistance package supported by the International Monetary Fund (IMF), the World Bank and the Asian Development Bank. \par \par \uc2  "In the eyes of the IMF and other nations, Indonesia is of very strategic importance to Asia, such a large economy with such a huge population. Indonesia ranks quite high in Asia. You can see the commitment by everybody in Asia," Low said. REUTERS \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb303eg1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
