\par\par \b \uc2  Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervenes \highlight\uc2 , sells dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Oct 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling spot dollars down from a high of 3,695/3,700 level on Friday morning, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the bank stepped in after the dollar traded above the psychological level of 3,700 throughout the morning. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more aggressive today. It was hitting every bids all the way down to 3,675 from 3,695/3,700 level," one local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "This seems to terrify people away from the 3,700 barrier for now," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The amount of dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not immediately known. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 3,670/80 at 0240 GMT, compared with an opening of 3,690/3,710. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtah048nc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
