\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Plunges/IMF -3: Bank Reform Needed \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 1997\par 14:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to be relatively small at $300 million and did succeed in weakening the dollar to around 3,700 rupiah level at the end of Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  Officials at Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, refused to confirm or deny the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports. \par \par \uc2  Because the volume of trading has been thin in the market in recent weeks, some optimists hold that pressure on the rupiah has been exaggerated. They also note that quarter-ending periods traditionally put added pressure on the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as companies move to square their dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  More bearish sentiment, however, focuses on monthly charges of between $5-$10 billion in dollar-denominated debt coming due. And with export-based companies apparently unwilling to let go of their dollars, there is the potential for continued downward pressure on the rupiah - and a growing number of loan defaults \par \par \uc2  With overnight lending rates still hovering well above 30%, there is concern that the health of Indonesia's overall financial system is facing a serious threat, adding credibility to the calls for IMF or World Bank assistance. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, for its part, does not have a strong record in regulating the nation's banking sector. The number of banks has grown to a dangerously high one of 239, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been unable over the past two years to force a consolidation. \par \par \uc2  Critics point to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inability to liquidate institutions such as Bank Pacific and Bank Yama as examples. Both institutions have extremely high levels of non-performing loans but remain in \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; many critics point to the banks' politically well-connected owners. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1227GMT \par \par \uc2  (CORRECTED 1232GMT) \par \par \uc2  1139 4204 62554 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dta607ht4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
