\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah remains weak, but off low. \b0\par\par\uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 30 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah remained weak against the dollar in thin early trading on Tuesday after falling to a historic low of 3,290, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said continued high corporate demand for dollars, either for hedging or to repay maturing papers, appeared to be one reason for sustained pressure on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  They said sufficient liquidity supply, coupled with the falling Malaysian ringgit, had added to rupiah woes. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 3,267/77 at 0400 GMT, compared with an opening of 3,205/15 on Tuesday. Tomorrow and today rupiah were at 3,260.25/67.25 and 3,261.0/68.0, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rupiah was around 17/18 percent and overnight swap was at par/0.1 point. Tom/next was at 0.2/0.5. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a shortage of dollar supply was another factor which boosted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  One foreign bank dealer said some offshore dollar buying and continued domestic hedging in the spot market had weakened the rupiah further to new lows on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  One chief dealer with a local bank said some corporates whose papers were maturing seemed to be borrowing from the interbank dollar market rather than buying spot dollars. \par \par \uc2  "Some seem to think it's too expensive to buy dollars from the spot market. So they just borrow short-term from the interbank market," he said, adding that this was reflected by rising overnight dollar rates to 25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said overnight dollar rose to as high as 40 percent on Monday, suggesting a short-term dollar liquidity problem. \par \par \uc2  "We also see some dollar purchases from some state banks. They won't buy it for speculation. This must be genuine dollar demand," the chief dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He viewed the current high dollar demand as a short-term liquidity problem which might be eased probably through some supply of dollar liquidity from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "An \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not be helpful because it would reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserve. Besides, the region is not in a good shape yet," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But a temporary dollar injection, sort of dollar lending to the interbank market, might help reduce the tightness in the market. This will not affect \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the price for the on-going high corporate demand was reflected in higher interbank rates for dollars or exchange rates, meaning rising dollars. \par \par \uc2  "But an improved dollar liquidity may help reduce pressure in the interbank market and the positive impact could probably spill over to the spot market," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "This could be a short-term way out while in the longer term we have to resort to fundamentals," he added. \par \par \uc2  One Singapore-based dealer said rises of the dollar appeared to be more Jakarta-driven, helped by relatively good supply of domestic liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "But rates are exaggerated due to thin volumes," he said, adding the rupiah was moving in tandem with the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  He said from the offshore-point of view offshore players were still long in cash-flows. \par \par \uc2  "It shouldn't be any problem for offshore to sell rupiah and buy spot dollars because they are very well funded," the dealer said, adding they were also well prepared in ringgit. \par \par \uc2  One-week swap was at 3.5/6.5, one-month at 25/35, two at 55/70, three at 90/105, six at 180/200 and one-year at 350/380. \par \par \uc2  -- Mantik Kusjanto (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9u01r7f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
