\par\par \b \uc2  =SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: Bank Indonesia Seen Facing Dilemma \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1997\par 13:55\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Tuesday's turmoil has emphasized to market participants\par that regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility is far from over. Daniel\par Lian, the head of Asian bond and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research at U.K.\par investment bank NatWest Markets, for example, expects the\par rupiah to resume its fall to levels around 3,000 rupiah to\par the U.S. dollar as interest rates fall.\par    But even if Bank Indonesia allows rates to ease in the\par short term to relieve the pressure on Indonesian banks and\par corporations, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise them to\par three-figure levels in the middle of September, Lian argues.\par    "Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily at the 2,660 rupiah\par to 2,690 rupiah level via the one-month forward Aug. 13.\par Bank Indonesia either has to roll (the contracts forward)\par into further month tenors or hope to mature them at a\par favorable spot rate," Lian said in a research report\par distributed Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is concerned about the impact of\par losses on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, it will have to\par keep the spot rate at around 2,700 rupiah, which means\par keeping interest rates high," he told Dow Jones.\par    "The hedge funds will start shorting the rupiah once\par again when interest rates come off, but it's not worth\par shorting at this level," he added.\par    Market participants are also expecting further falls in\par other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Andrew Fung, regional Treasury\par economist at Standard Chartered Bank, is targeting a level\par of 2.85 ringgit to the U.S. dollar for the end of September,\par as trade imbalances and worries about the finance sector's\par exposure to property undermine confidence in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Privately many regional analysts and traders speak of\par 3.00 ringgit to the U.S. dollar as a more realistic level.\par And if the ringgit falls that far, they say, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore may be prepared to allow the\par Singapore dollar to drift as low as S$1.60 to the U.S.\par dollar to maintain the city state's competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  08-26-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0755EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt8q01t8g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
