\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht drop depresses S.E.Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 1997\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 22 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid once more on Friday as the Thai baht fell to record lows, spurring fresh buying of the dollar across the board. \par \par \uc2  The baht hit a new record low of 34.10 to the dollar onshore in the afternoon after heavy commercial demand for dollars and nagging concerns about Thailand's economic and political outlook pushed the baht through the key 33 level in early trade. \par \par \uc2  "When the baht breached the 33 level, everyone lost confidence and wanted to unwind the baht as quickly as possible," a Bangkok dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 34.10/40 to the dollar at 0855 GMT against 33.13/32 five hours earlier. Offshore baht was at 33.65/80 against 32.70/32.80. \par \par \uc2  Concern that Thailand's shrinking foreign reserves would be affected by big forward swap contracts carried by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also hurt sentiment for the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it had $23.4 billion in forward swap contracts that are due over the next 12 months, of which $8.6 billion are onshore and $14.8 billion offshore. \par \par \uc2  The forward contracts were taken to defend the baht during massive speculative attacks in May. \par \par \uc2  "With 33 being broken, the sky's the limit. It's in uncharted territory," the head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  He said the baht looked set to hit 35 to the dollar and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the slide. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupiah recovered from its lows but remained weak as players covered short dollar positions ahead of the weekend and local companies sought to hedge their positions. \par \par \uc2  "The funds are buying the dollar again after liquidating their positions above the 2,900 level," the Singapore dealer said. Sentiment was also depressed by Standard and Poor's announcement on Thursday that it had revised the ratings outlook on Indonesian banks to negative from stable, he added. \par \par \uc2  Reports of a run on deposits at one of Indonesia's banks were also affecting the market, he said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,700/10 after falling to a low of 2,755 against 2,675/75 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese bank dealer in Jakarta said the rupiah could strengthen through the 2,700 level again as the outlook for liquidity remained tight. \par \par \uc2  "Liquidity is still the main concern. Operators are also preparing for Monday because the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forward \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will mature," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit surrendered early gains and fell sharply on spillover from the rupiah and baht, though thin volumes and wide spreads continued to exaggerate activity. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at 2.7685/715 to the dollar after reaching a high of 2.7430 earlier, against 2.7650/700 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slid back through the 1.50 to the U.S. dollar level and was quoted at 1.5040/50 at 0855 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "But the pace will be slower as the market is looking more favourably at the Singapore dollar than the other regionals," a dealer said, citing strong Singapore export figures announced on Wednesday and an upward revision of its 1997 growth forecast. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended firmer on inflows of arbitrage money and as exporters and other companies converted foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits to pesos following recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to tighten liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The peso finished at 29.85 to the dollar against Thursday's close of 29.885. \par \par \uc2  In Taiwan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prolonged defence of the T$28.727 level in the face of offshore speculative pressure finally dampened demand for U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar ended virtually unchanged at T$28.725. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8m00roy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
