\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  rupiah down again, no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . [CORRECTED 12:20 GMT] \b0\par\par\uc2  By Raju Gopalakrishnan \par \uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 15 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah was hit again on Friday as investors panicked in the aftermath of its float and pushed the unit to yet another historic low against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  By the close of trading in Jakarta, the rupiah was at 2,880/2,910 against the dollar, which was about four percent weaker (corrects from "more than one percent weaker") than the 2,770/90 open but off a 2,960 low. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they waited in vain for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restore confidence. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band on Thursday, effectively floating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said it reserved the right to step into the market if deemed necessary. \par \par \uc2  Edwin Png, head of treasury for Bank of America in Jakarta, said the steep falls had made the market jittery. \par \par \uc2  "I have housewives calling me up to ask about the rate," he said in the early afternoon. "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now or else I see the rate going up to 3,000 later in the day and 3,200 next week." \par \par \uc2  "They should do both. They should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and they should tighten liquidity." \par \par \uc2  In the event, the rate did not fall that far despite the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But dealers and analysts said the tone of the market was weak because many Indonesian companies were scrambling to hedge their dollar exposures. \par \par \uc2  They added that volumes were thin because most investors squared positions ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  Most however said the panic in the rupiah would be short-lived and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would soon trade at more realistic levels, perhaps some time next week. \par \par \uc2  "We'll see the bottom end of the rupiah start to appear fairly soon," said Kevin Evans, senior analyst at ANZ Securities in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "I'm looking for the rupiah to come in at the end of this year somewhere between 2,700 and 2,800. We'll see it recover somewhat and then see a stable cycle after that." \par \par \uc2  "There is some nervousness onshore because a lot of corporates had not fully hedged their dollar liability and thus we may indeed go to the 3,000 level before the rupiah begins to recover towards more sustainable levels in line with its basic fundamentals," Bill Belchere, the head of Asian fixed income research at Merrill Lynch, told Reuters Financial Television. \par \par \uc2  "We do believe the fundamentals are sound, Indonesia is not like Thailand in any way," he added. "However, it's a very nervous market, you cannot contain the effect of spillover in the medium-term. However, in the longer-term we are sure Indonesia has very fine economic prospects and we would see the rupiah somewhere between 2,600 and 2,700 to the dollar." \par \par \uc2  The prolonged spell of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness which has hit Southeast Asia began in May with attacks on the Thai baht. Thailand was forced to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July and has said it has received pledges worth $17 billion from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and Asian nations. \par \par \uc2  The IMF has welcomed Indonesia's decision to allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to float, saying the move would allow the country's economy to continue its recent impressive performance. \par \par \uc2  "In present circumstances, a floating exchange rate will enhance the effectiveness of macroeconomic policies aimed at sustaining high rates of growth with financial stability," said Stanley Fischer, acting managing director of the IMF, in a statement issued in Washington. \par \par \uc2  Fischer called Indonesia's decision timely and said it came partly in response to turbulence on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. He said floating the rupiah was "in line with Bank Indonesia's steady progress toward greater exchange rate flexibility, particularly over the last two years". \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8f016sj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
