\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Rupiah plunges,dealers look for  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Raju Gopalakrishnan \par \uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 15 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah plunged further on Friday, the day after it was floated, and dealers said they were looking to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and restore market confidence. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to a new record low of 2,915 to the dollar by early afternoon from its opening level of 2,770/90 after liquidity suddenly eased from a record overnight rate of 125 percent to about 30 percent. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate determines whether it is profitable for investors to borrow rupiah to speculate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "At this rate, borrowing costs are just about five rupiah (per dollar). It's extremely profitable for people to speculate, since there are swings of about 100 rupiah in the spot rate," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Edwin Png, head of treasury for Bank of America in Jakarta, said the market was losing confidence. \par \par \uc2  "I have housewives calling me up to ask about the rate," he said. "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now or else I see the rate going up to 3,000 later in the day and 3,200 next week. \par \par \uc2  "They should do both. They should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and they should tighten liquidity." \par \par \uc2  Other dealers said the easing in liquidity appeared to have come about after some state-owned banks offered money in the market and added that that implied the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was being inconsistent in its policy. \par \par \uc2  "They said yesterday that they would maintain tightness, but it doesn't look as if they are doing so," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate shot up in the morning because of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday with about $500 million. The money became due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad said on Thursday, less than an hour after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  removed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band and effectively floated the rupiah, that tight monetary and fiscal policies were in place and any changes would depend on developments. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sudradjad Djiwandono said although the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band had been scrapped, authorities reserved the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they deemed necessary. The band had determined at what levels the bank would step into the market. \par \par \uc2  "Of course Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep developments on course, to smooth the adaptment period," he said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But State Planning Minister Ginanjar Kartasasmita appeared to hint that authorities would allow the market to decide the level of the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "If they (speculators) see the government will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we hope they will reduce their speculative activity," he told reporters on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Our fundamental economy is sound. We are entering a new era of market principles. It is the correct time for the government to carry out such a policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the International Monetary Fund hailed the move to float the rupiah, saying it was good for the economy. \par \par \uc2  "In present circumstances, a floating exchange rate will enhance the effectiveness of macroeconomic policies aimed at sustaining high rates of growth with financial stability," said Stanley Fischer, acting managing director of the IMF, in a statement issued in Washington. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8f0137u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
