\par\par \b \uc2  INDONESIAN STOCKS - factors to watch - Aug 15. \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 15 (Reuter) - Following are some of the main factors likely to affect Indonesian stocks on Friday: \par \par \uc2  * On Thursday, the Dow Jones industrial average ended up 13.71 points at 7,942.03. \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian overnight money jumped to 125 percent on Friday from 50.0/60.0 percent in early trade on extremely tight liquidity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sudradjad Djiwandono said on Thursday that the bank's decision to abandon its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was taken because other countries in the region had floated their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  MARKET \par \par \uc2  * On Thursday, the Jakarta composite index closed down 15.59 points, or 2.37 percent, at 643.01 points on an announcement by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it was scrapping its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  * The Indonesian rupiah was quoted at 2,775.00/95.00 against the dollar at 0200 GMT compared with 2,770.00/90.00 at the opening. \par \par \uc2  STOCKS TO WATCH \par \par \uc2  * Banks, particularly small banks including Unibank, Bank Servitia and Bank Pikko, as they may be hit by the higher cost of funds because of high overnight call money rates. \par \par \uc2  * Other banks, including Bank International Indonesia and Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the abolishment of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band could hit earnings from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities. \par \par \uc2  * Cigarette maker Gudang Garam, BDNI and Astra following announcements of first half net profits. \par \par \uc2  * Telecommunications firm Telkom and Indosat on a Neraca newspaper report that the government did not plan to hike telephone fees despite the rupiah's depreciation against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364 Fax: (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- E-Mail: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8f01320\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
