\par\par \b \uc2  INDONESIA PALM OIL RISES ON WEAKER RUPIAH. \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 14 (Reuter) - Indonesian palm oil prices rose in late trading on Thursday after the rupiah's steep plunge when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said a tender was done at 1,285 rupiah/kg for 500 tonnes of palm oil in North Sumatran city of Medan in the afternoon against the last tender at 1,246 rupiah/kg on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Palm olein was slightly higher at 1,496-1,500 rupiah/kg in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "People are holding back positions because they want to wait for further developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will no longer announce its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conversion bands with immediate effect. Spot rupiah was ranging between 2,750 and 2,790 in the afternoon, with some players seen cashing out from dollars. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah fell to a low 2,800 in thin volume before recovering to 2,760/70 at 0810 GMT from an opening of 2,648/58. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said they largerly ignored the Malaysian palm oil output for July which was projected to to have risen 4.5 percent to 823,000 tonnes according to private forecaster Ivan Wong. \par \par \uc2  "Such figure has been widely expected so it does not have any impact on the Indonesian market," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected to see some adjustment in palm olein prices on Friday after palm oil's rise. "At least olein prices should be quoted at 1,550, otherwise it will not be profitable to do business," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  -- 