\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah dives, depressing others. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par 12:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 14 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah's steep drop after Jakarta announced a more flexible exchange rate regime dragged down other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement that it would stop posting a daily dollar/rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, removing the parameters within which it steps into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, sent the rupiah diving by over as five percent from its levels late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The timing of the action by the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as a surprise a day after it raised rates and sold dollars to keep the rupiah within its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  "Theoretically, it's a free float," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sudradjad Djiwandono told Reuters Financial Television. \par \par \uc2  "But of course Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep developments on course," he said, in order to smooth the period of adapting to the move. \par \par \uc2  "You can also call it a managed float without a band." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell as low as 2,810 during the day against its opening around 2,648/58. It was quoted at 2,760/70 at 0925 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah appeared to have stabilised temporarily, but the reaction of players in London and New York would shape its direction. \par \par \uc2  Analysts hailed the Indonesian move as a welcome response to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and economic turmoil in the region, which has highlighted the need for greater exchange rate flexibility. \par \par \uc2  "It's much more prudent than widening the band and giving the market a fresh target to aim at," said Desmond Supple, head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at BZW Asia in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Doggedly defending the band would whittle away at the country's reserves, raise interest rates and slow growth." \par \par \uc2  Other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which started the day on relatively firm footing following the dollar's overnight drop against the majors, fell along with the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Comments by Malaysian Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim exacerbated pressure on the ringgit. He said the government was concerned about the sharp rise in Malaysia's June trade deficit to 2.8 billion ringgit and it may use taxes or fiscal measures to cut imports and stimulate exports. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit fell from a high of 2.7530 to the dollar after the remarks. It was quoted at 2.7665/715 against 2.7815/45 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A government official denied later rumours that Malaysia planned to cut the statutory reserve requirement of banks. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore slipped back through the 1.51 level against the U.S. dollar and the Thai baht also came under pressure, partly from commercial dollar demand, but dealers said activity was muted. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso recovered from an early low of 29.620 to the dollar, but ended weak at 29.49 on concerns about regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. \par \par \uc2  Manila traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not step in to defend the peso, but kept its offer rate for the dollar 10 centavos above the best offer. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained fragile after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its overnight borrowing rate by four percentage points to 14 percent amid persistent demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar finished fractionally firmer at T$28.725 on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8e019p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
