\par\par \b \uc2  INDONESIA LATE RUBBER EASES ON  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY \highlight\uc2  FALL. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 14 (Reuter) - Indonesian tyre-grade SIR20 rubber prices eased in late trading on Thursday following the government's move to float the rupiah, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Our prime concern now is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We've seen prices slightly softening because of a weaker rupiah. I believe prices can drop to as low as 40.00 (U.S. cents/lb)," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah had stabilised at sharply lower levels in late trading on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped its band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will no longer announce its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conversion bands with immediate effect. Spot rupiah was ranging between 2,750 and 2,790 in the afternoon, with some players seen cashing out from dollars. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah fell to a low of 2,800 in thin volume before recovering to 2,760/70 at 0810 GMT from an opening of 2,648/58. \par \par \uc2  Rubber traders said a weaker rupiah had prompted buyers to put pressure on the prices. \par \par \uc2  "Buyers will be making use of the situation by asking for cheaper rubber. The market was very quiet until late in the afternoon as most people are still in the dark about what's going to happen next with the rupiah," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Traders said demand was weak while supply was generally good in most centres. \par \par \uc2  "Prices are already weak because of the poor demand while traders are taking a wait-and-see position today. If the rupiah is getting weaker, then the level of 40.00 is not impossible," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  He said the market would be closely monitoring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements in the next few days. \par \par \uc2  Traders said offer prices were quoted at 42.00 for November/December shipment fob Medan, 42.25 fob Palembang, Surabaya and Padang for October shipment and 41.50 fob Padang for September shipmment. \par \par \uc2  -- Lewa Pardomuan (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- E-mail: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8e019oy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
