\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Indonesia floats rupiah,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  plunges. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Raju Gopalakrishnan \par \uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par 10:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 14 (Reuter) - Indonesia floated the rupiah on Thursday, triggering a steep 100-point fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar and taking it deep into uncharted waters. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , announced it was lifting the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band with immediate effect, abandoning the parameters under which the bank steps into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "Theoretically, it's a free float," bank governor Sudradjad Djiwandono told Reuters Financial Television in an interview. \par \par \uc2  "But of course Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep developments on course," he said, in order to smoothen the period of adapting to the new move. \par \par \uc2  "You can also call it a managed float without a band." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah dived on the news by more than 100 points from an opening of 2,648/58 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In mid-afternoon, it was trading at 2,750/60 and appeared to have temporarily stabilised, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The bank had last fixed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,378/2,682 on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes the latest Southeast Asian nation to succumb to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressures which have been afflicting the region since early July. \par \par \uc2  On July 1, the rupiah was trading at around 2,430 per dollar although subsequent pressures pulled it to a record low of 2,665 on July 21 and to 2,682 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Djiwandono said the Thai baht and the Philippine peso had been floated since speculative attacks on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  began, while the Malaysian ringgit and the Singapore dollar were being traded without any pre-announced limits. \par \par \uc2  "We are a regional market now. We are moving together," Djiwandono said. \par \par \uc2  "In the last few weeks Indonesia is the only one which had a band. It's the only one defending the rupiah," he said, adding that maintaining that position would be increasingly difficult. \par \par \uc2  "We are adjusting to the new realities," he said. "The new reality in the ASEAN (Association of South East Asian Nations) region is floating (\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 )." \par \par \uc2  Economists said the move was a positive one. \par \par \uc2  "It's much more prudent than widening the band and giving the market a fresh target to aim at," said Desmond Supple, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist at BZW Asia in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Doggedly defending the band would whittle away at the country's reserves, raise interest rates and slow growth." \par \par \uc2  He said it was not surprising that the rupiah had plunged on the announcement but added that there was scope for recovery later. \par \par \uc2  "We are going to see substantial over-shooting," Supple said. "But it (the announcement) lays the conditions for reversal of the rupiah in the long-term and bring it back to a semblance of fair value." \par \par \uc2  Some market-watchers said it was possible that after abandoning the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could introduce some form of mild capital controls to limit the scope for speculation. \par \par \uc2  Both Malaysia and Singapore have adopted systems which prevent sizeable non-trade forward transactions. \par \par \uc2  But Djiwandono said there would be no move to introduce exchange controls on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "Why should we control?" he said when asked if there was a possibility of any such move." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8e019la\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
