\par\par \b \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH FALLS TO HISTORIC LOW BUT STABLE. \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 14 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah stabilised against the dollar at a historic low in morning trade on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped the announcement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conversion bands, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah stabilised at 2,750/80 at 0350 GMT after strengthening to 2,635 in early morning from an opening of 2,648/58 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers however said the market remained jittery after the announcement, which economists said implied a managed float. \par \par \uc2  Longer-term swap rates fell after the announcement. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will no longer announce its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conversion bands with immediate effect. \par \par \uc2  "The government has decided effective from today, August 14, the announcement of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conversion bands, which are usually announced at 3 p.m. local time (0800 GMT), will be abolished," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  One state bank dealer said the statement did not imply the abolishment of the band but only its announcement. \par \par \uc2  "This implies that the band will be invisible, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time it wants," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The state bank dealer said the move would help the country safeguard its valuable reserves. \par \par \uc2  "It's a sort of managed float," said Desmond Supple, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist at BZW Asia in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Basically Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time. It's a good move. It's much more prudent than widening the band and giving the market a fresh target to aim at." \par \par \uc2  "Doggedly defending the band would whittle away at the country's reserves, raise interest rates and slow growth." \par \par \uc2  He said it was not surprising that the rupiah had plunged on the announcement but said there was scope for recovery later. \par \par \uc2  "We are going to see substantial over-shooting," Supple said. "But it (the announcement) lays the conditions for reversal of the rupiah in the long-term and bring it back to a semblance of fair value." \par \par \uc2  The last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band announced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday was 2,378/2,682 and the conversion band at 2,629/2,677. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8e019ho\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
