\par\par \b \uc2  BANK INDONESIA TO ABOLISH RUPIAH BAND ANNOUNCEMENT. \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 14 (Reuter) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Indonesia, said on Thursday it will no longer announce its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conversion bands with immediate effect. \par \par \uc2  "The government has decided effective from today, August 14, the announcement of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and conversion bands, which are usually announced at 3 p.m. local time (0800 GMT) will be abolished," Djakaria, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "Export bill discount facilities for Thursday remain as usual, using rates from August 13 (Wednesday)," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Bank note transactions with Bank Indonesia will stay but the time will be changed to 2 p.m. to 3 p.m. local time with rates to be announced at 2 p.m. local time on the same day," he said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's announcement said only the announcement of the band was being abolished. It did not give further details but economists said the move implied a managed float. \par \par \uc2  "It's a sort of managed float," said Desmond Supple, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist at BZW Asia. "Basically Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time." \par \par \uc2  Others said the bank would work on invisible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  parameters, which would allow it to step into the market at any time of its choosing. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8e019fv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngbli