\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2 /Volatile-2: Using All Monetary Tools \b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 1997\par 12:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia Governor Soedradjad Djiwandono said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in order to maintain stability. \par \par \uc2  Soedradjad repeated a theme he has been using often in recent days that 'Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use all of its monetary tools, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain stability' in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor's comments were given during a hastily assembled press conference following the flotation of the Indonesian rupiah earlier Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah has plunged around 5% after the scrapping of Bank Indonesia's 12% dollar-rupiah trading band. At 1000 GMT (6:00 a.m. EDT) the U.S. dollar is quoted at 2,830 rupiah, up from 2,644 rupiah immediately before the scrapping of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1023GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8e061so\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
