\par\par \b \uc2  =SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: $200M Sold In Rupiah's Defense \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1997\par 13:24\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At an early afternoon press briefing, however, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Soedradjad Djiwandono made his position clear\par to local reporters. Bank Indonesia, he said, would use "all\par monetary instruments available to stabilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market."\par    At around 0600 GMT, the U.S. dollar penetrated the top\par of its permitted band against the rupiah, reaching a high of\par 2,682 rupiah bid.\par    Just an hour and a half later, the U.S. dollar was sent\par plunging to an intraday low of 2,630 rupiah on what traders\par said was massive Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  involving the\par sale of around $200 million.\par    "Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is throwing good money after bad.\par Naturally, the market will carry on pressing against the\par upper limit of the band," said the head of regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at a major U.S.-based international investment\par bank in Singapore, who estimated that Bank Indonesia had\par spent around $200 million buying rupiah in the spot market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "This isn't just speculation, there is a lot of genuine\par demand for dollars from Indonesian banks and corporations.\par For years, there has been a low volatility carry trade, and\par now with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moving around all over the place,\par people want to cover themselves," he explained.\par    In the past, with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk eliminated by a tightly\par managed gradual depreciation, Indonesian banks have been\par able to borrow in low-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as yen or\par U.S. dollars and relend at a much higher yield in rupiah.\par Recently, threatened with seeing their margins wiped out by\par heightened \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility, thay have rushed to cover\par themselves by buying dollars for rupiah, forcing the\par Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down still further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  08-13-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0724EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt8d01pj2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
