\par\par \b \uc2  =SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Bank Indonesia Stands Firm On Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1997\par 13:09\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--It was the turn of the Indonesian\par rupiah to come under massive selling pressure on Wednesday,\par in yet another turbulent day for Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets.\par    But unlike other regional central banks, Bank Indonesia\par stood firm and defended its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a move that left\par analysts and traders doubting the wisdom of the nation's\par policy.\par    Proprietary traders at offshore banks began selling the\par rupiah for U.S. dollars in early morning trading as rumors\par swept the Singapore market that Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was preparing\par to abandon its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  band in favor of a freely\par floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    On Tuesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore had\par followed the Malaysian authorities in indicating that it was\par prepared to accept a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . With Indonesian\par analysts arguing publicly that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wasn't a viable\par policy, many offshore traders assumed that the regional move\par toward freely floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was now irrestible.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Indonesia, they thought, was on the verge of following\par its Association of Southeast Asian Nations peers and\par jettisoning its permitted trading band of 2,378 rupiah to\par 2,682 rupiah to the U.S. dollar.\par    "Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has no need to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Daragh\par Maher, a Singapore-based economist at Dutch-owned investment\par bank ING Barings.\par    "In fact, in the long run, floating the rupiah could be\par beneficial; it would allow Bank Indonesia to lower interest\par rates," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  08-13-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0709EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt8d01pig\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
