\par\par \b \uc2  Spotlight on the rupiah, Asian regionals pressured. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Raju Gopalakrishnan \par \uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1997\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 13 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah took centre stage in a still nervous Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, plunging to a historic low and forcing a defensive interest rate rise and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to step in after the rupiah shrugged off the rate rise and dropped to the lower limit of its 12 percent trading band. \par \par \uc2  It fell to a low of 2,682 to the dollar in the afternoon before recovering on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 2,640/50. The bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, the parameters outside of which it will enter the market, was last pegged at 2,378/2,682. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could well be a losing battle given the continuing weakness in all Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's useless for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bearish market," said Jimmy Koh, regional economist for the I.D.E.A. research consultancy. He noted that the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent some $8.8 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures when the ringgit was under attack earlier this month, but with little to show for its efforts. \par \par \uc2  The rate rise came as a bit of a surprise as the very rates which were cut last Friday by 50 basis points were raised 100 basis points, so on a net basis policy is tighter now. \par \par \uc2  "They are raising short-term rates but keeping the long-term rates, which determine lending and spending behaviour in the economy, at current levels," said Manu Bhaskaran, Group Head of Research at SocGen Crosby. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a clear strategy and I think they will use short-term rates where necessary to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Singapore dollar remained under pressure but recouped some of its losses on talk of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  near its low of 1.5175 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  It was at a late 1.5100 where dealers said there are strong bids for U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  They said local banks were seen selling the U.S. dollar near its highs earlier, often an indication of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence, but no confirmation was available. \par \par \uc2  A European bank dealer said the U.S. dollar would be bought on any dips to 1.5100 or 1.5050 for an eventual move up to 1.53. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit moved narrowly but showed persistent signs of weakness and dealers said the market was likely to take a crack at the 2.80 level, a low not seen since the ringgit was officially floated in 1973. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/ringgit could still reach 2.80 and probably go above that level," said a Malaysian bank dealer. "But I'm expecting some resistance at 2.7850." \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at 2.7775 to the dollar against 2.7645/75 at the close of Kuala Lumpur trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht started easier but regained its composure to trade at a late 31.430 onshore and 31.350 offshore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were some sales of dollars offshore ahead of the expected mid-August maturity of short baht forward positions, established when the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under speculative attack three months ago. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso remained weak as banks bought up the dollar in volatile regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Corporate customers are also looking to buy dollars at the moment and that was keeping the pressure on the peso, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The peso was at 28.85 against its previous close at 28.66. Manila traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have sold dollars at the 28.70/28.78 levels earlier but no confirmation was available. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar remained weak but fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tight liquidity in domestic money markets helped limit any decline. It was at a late 28.726 per U.S. dollar, little changed from Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8d017l2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
