\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Indonesian markets weaken, rupiah plunges. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Raju Gopalakrishnan \par \uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1997\par 13:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 13 (Reuter) - Indonesia's markets went through another harrowing session on Wednesday with the rupiah plunging to a record low before recovering on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the stock market closing markedly weaker. \par \par \uc2  The fallout from continuing weakness in South East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove the rupiah to a historic low against the dollar for the second time in four weeks, forcing Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Jakarta stock market composite index closed down 0.66 percent at 658.60 points in response to the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and higher interest rates announced by Bank Indonesia in a vain bid to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  The index has fallen by more than 50 points since the beginning of the month on a combination of high interest rates, new controls on margin finance and a slew of rights issues. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to a low of 2,682 to the dollar in the afternoon despite the higher rates before recovering on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 2,650/80. \par \par \uc2  The bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, the parameters outside of which it will enter the market, was maintained at 2,378/2,682 at the daily fixing, indicating authorities were not immediately considering any change in policy. \par \par \uc2  There was no indication of how much money the bank had pumped into the market. Analysts said it could well be a losing battle given the continuing weakness in all South East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and their susceptibility to contagion. \par \par \uc2  "It's useless for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bearish market," said Jimmy Koh, regional economist for the I.D.E.A. research consultancy. He noted that the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent some $8.8 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures when the ringgit was under attack earlier this month, but with little to show for its efforts. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit slumped to a 42-month low of 2.7930 against the dollar on Tuesday and continued to be weak on Wednesday. Its weakness has spread to Indonesia, compounding earlier contagion from the Thai baht, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "First it was the tom yam effect," said Koh. "Now it's the asam laksa effect," referring to a fiery Thai soup and popular Malaysian noodles-in-soup dish. The fallout from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil in Thailand and Malaysia has hit all regional markets. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Bank Indonesia raised interest rates for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates of all maturities by 100 basis points. The move makes it more expensive for investors to borrow rupiah, which could then be used for speculation. \par \par \uc2  But Koh said the raising of rates could only be used as a short-term measure and forecast a further fall in the rupiah as domestic corporates began to hedge their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks. \par \par \uc2  "Corporates here are not used to hedging risk, but with things the way they are, they have no option," Koh said. "That will affect the rupiah further." \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said the contagion effect was exacerbated by a newspaper report quoting a leading local economist as saying that the rupiah should be allowed to find its own level. \par \par \uc2  Sjahrir, an economist and brokerage firm owner, told the Kompas daily that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  need not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that the market would ultimately decide a fair value for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "According to me, just let the rupiah fall to 2,700 or 2,800. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have to do anything. Once they (speculators) realise the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't done anything, the dollar is already overvalued," Sjahrir was quoted as saying. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's previous historic low was 2,665 on July 21. \par \par \uc2  Donald Hanna, an economist with Goldman Sachs in Hong Kong, said raising interest rates was however a sensible move to curb the rupiah volatility. \par \par \uc2  "The economy is not as weak as in Thailand," he said. "There is more resilience to higher interest rates. There is no fundamental reason for the rupiah to weaken." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8d017is\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
