\par\par \b \uc2  BANK INDONESIA DEFENDS BAND, RUPIAH STABILISES. \b0\par\par\uc2 699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 13 (Reuter) - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  defended its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band on Wednesday after the rupiah fell to a historic low, erasing much of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses by the close of the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars in the spot market although some said the bank was also seen in the one-month forward market. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah bounced back sharply to 2,620 from a historic low of 2,682 before easing back to 2,650/60 at 0945 GMT at the close of trading in Jakarta. The rupiah opened at 2,643/50. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow and today rupiah closed at 2,644/54 and 2,665/68, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its dollar-rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band unchanged on Wednesday at 2,378/2,682 but raised its conversion band to 2,629/2,677 from 2,616/2,664 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market had speculated that the band would be widened or possibly removed altogether after the rupiah plunged before recovering on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were not clear how much money the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had pumped into the market to calm nervous operators. \par \par \uc2  "But for sure we are going to see a tightened money market on Friday. The move will result in rupiah scarcity," one said. \par \par \uc2  The local bank dealer said operators had immediately locked in longer-term liquidity available now. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to defend the band with the help of the short-term interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  The bank raised interest rates for bilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates (SBIs) of all maturities by 100 basis points. Overnight rates were raised to 15.0 percent, two-to-six day SBIs to 16.0 percent, one-week to 10.5, two-week to 11.0, one-month to 11.625, three to 11.5, six to 12.125 and one-year to 12.75. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also remained absent from the short-term securities (SBPUs) market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its bilateral SBI rates for papers above one-week by 50 basis points last Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market showed signs of stabilisation. \par \par \uc2  However, renewed pressure spilling over from neighbouring countries knocked the rupiah down further, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to impose a tighter money policy to contain speculation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said heavy selling of the rupiah on Wednesday was triggered on contagion effect from the Singapore dollar and the Malaysian ringgit and on comments by a local economist. \par \par \uc2  Sjahrir, an economist and brokerage firm owner, was quoted in the Kompas daily as saying the market would ultimately decide a fair value for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "According to me, just let the rupiah fall to 2,700 or 2,800. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have to do anything. Once they (speculators) realise the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't done anything, the dollar is already overvalued," Sjahrir was quoted as saying. \par \par \uc2  But an economist with one of the country's state-owned banks said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to continue defending the band. \par \par \uc2  "We all know that there is nothing wrong with the economy or the country's fundamentals. But speculators keep trying. The bank has to give some certainty for the people," the economist said. \par \par \uc2  "There is little use of pointing to fundamentals. We just have to wait until the storm is over," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said swap rates remained high as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen mainly in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  Overnight swap was at 1.05/1.25 and tom/next at 1.5/1.8. \par \par \uc2  One local bank dealer said offshore operators were seen biddish in one-week and one-month swaps, pushing them to end at 7.5/8.5 and 30.0/40.0 points, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Two-month swap was at 55.0/61.0, three at 72.0/78.0 and six at 130.0/136.0 points. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money was last at 20.0/25.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month in the forward market with some one billion dollars. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8d017hn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
