\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia/Dlr Breaks/Band -2: Dlr Hit 2,685 At 0606 GMT \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1997\par 08:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar broke through the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weak end of the rupiah's trading band at 0606 GMT (2:06 a.m. EDT), but then retreated to the 2,678 rupiah level almost immediately. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is now trading right at the rupiah's weak end at 2,681.50 rupiah at 0626 GMT (2:26 a.m. EDT). \par \par \uc2  Local traders said they have seen no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as yet, but there remain no bids currently above the 2,872 rupiah level locally. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say that they expect continued downward pressure on the rupiah later in the day, which will pose serious questions to Bank Indonesia as to whether it wants to defend the rupiah's current 12% trading band, or let it move to a free float. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are looking to Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily fixing of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 0800 GMT (4:00 a.m. EDT) for a signal of where Bank Indonesia is headed. The band is currently set at 2,378 rupiah to 2,682 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0634GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8d05zlo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
