\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia: Shrs Close Lower Due To Rupiah's Biggest Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1997\par 12:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--Shares on the Jakarta Stock Exchange (JSX) closed lower Wednesday as investors continued to be distracted by the intense speculative attacks against the Indonesian rupiah by both offshore and local dealers. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was pushed above the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band, sparking widespread reports of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  These attacks kept trading on the Jakarta exchange very light, with little buying sentiment, market participants said. Dealers noted that the cheapness of many Indonesian shares has lent some support. \par \par \uc2  'The market didn't react very negatively when the rupiah penetrated through the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level as current prices are already very cheap,' a head trader at a local brokerage house said. \par \par \uc2  The JSX index finished down 4.343 points Wednesday to 658.604 points as losers outnumbered gainers 78 to 46, with 64 shares unchanged. Volume was 145 million shares with a value of 235 billion rupiah according to a local securities company. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar broke through the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weak end of the rupiah's trading band of 2,683 rupiah at 0606 GMT (2:06 a.m EDT), but settled down later following reports of Bank Indonesia selling dollars in the spot market to support the rupiah. The dollar traded at 2,655 rupiah at 0930 GMT (5:30 a.m. EDT). \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that shares on the JSX have been discounted on an average of between 15% and 20% from what is seen as their fair value amid the current index slide of 10% over the last two weeks. But concerns over the high interest rates brought on by a liquidity squeeze has killed major support for the market. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia increased by 100 basis points rates on its Sertifikat Bank Indonesia money market certificates. \par \par \uc2  A head broker with a local securities company added that the sluggish trend was also boosted by the falls on other major bourses. Brokers said tobacco and banking stocks contributed significantly to the share-index falls but the rise in cement stocks have offset the index from falling further. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1030GMT \par \par \uc2  5055 55109 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8d05xe5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
