\par\par \b \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH TUMBLES ON CONTAGION EFFECT. \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 19 (Reuter) - The Indonesian rupiah tumbled to 2,646/49 against the dollar at 0145 GMT on Tuesday from an opening of 2,610/20 on falls in the Malaysian ringgit and the Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said falls in the ringgit and the Singapore dollar spilled over to the rupiah at the opening, driving the rupiah down to a low of 2,655 before it recovered on local dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  "It's the contagion effect again. The market is a bit nervous, with spreads trending to widen again. But volume was moderate," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said stop-loss limits were triggered after the rupiah fell through the 2,620 level. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said operators remained nervous and cautious, waiting for further developments on the ringgit and the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar dipped briefly to 1.50 to the U.S. dollar after an official of the country's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate was at an appropriate level. \par \par \uc2  An official of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) said the Singapore dollar's level was appropriate to what was happening in the market. \par \par \uc2  The official said the U.S. dollar had been rising in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets recently and the Singapore dollar had depreciated by about five percent against the U.S. unit since the start of 1997. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 2,378/2,682 but raised the conversion band to 2,588/2,636 on Monday from 2,573/2,621 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8c01e5d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
