\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Mins See Exports Boost From Rupiah Fall -Newspaper \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1997\par 11:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (AP-Dow Jones)--The Indonesian government hopes a recent drop in the value of the rupiah, Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , can boost its non-oil exports, especially natural resources-based products. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's Jakarta Post quoted two ministers as saying non-oil exports will reach a target of $55 billion this year because of the weakened rupiah. \par \par \uc2  'Depreciation (of the rupiah against the dollar) has a positive impact on our exports,' said Hartarto Sastrosoenarto, coordinating minister for production and distribution. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Minister of Industry Tunky Ariwibowo said the weaker rupiah would particularly help exports of agricultural and forestry products and minerals. \par \par \uc2  However, it also would affect exports of products with a high import content, especially manufactured products like machinery components and steel products. \par \par \uc2  Tunky said non-oil exports grew by only 9% in the first five months of this year, 1 percentage point lower than the growth in the same period last year. \par \par \uc2  'With this depreciation, we are optimistic about achieving our non-oil exports target of $55 billion for this year,' said Tunky. \par \par \uc2  Soedradjad Djiwandono, governor of Bank Indonesia, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has warned that speculation in the rupiah would continue for some time until tranquility returns to the region's financial markets. \par \par \uc2  He expressed hope that the assaults on the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will die down when the Thai baht stabilizes. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to spend about $1 billion last month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the value of the rupiah, as it bottomed at 2,662.50 rupiah to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0932GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8505qct\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
